# Ultrarapid long-read genome analysis pipeline

A GPU-enabled Snakemake workflow for rapid germline variant calling, annotation, prioritization, and interactive review from Oxford Nanopore whole-genome sequencing data.

The pipeline jointly analyzes:

- SNVs and small indels with Clair3
- Structural variants with Sniffles2
- Large copy-number variants using mosdepth and CNVkit
- Joint SNV/SV phasing and BAM haplotagging with LongPhase
- Variant annotation using offline VEP, ClinVar, gnomAD, MANE, SVAFotate, DGV, and dosage-sensitivity resources
- Candidate prioritization for rare-disease analysis
- Interactive IGV.js reports for SNVs/indels, SVs, and CNVs
- A combined tabbed HTML report containing all candidate variant classes

## Workflow overview

| Stage | Software | Output |
|---|---|---|
| Optional BAM merge | samtools | Merged and indexed BAM |
| SNV/indel calling | Clair3 | PASS small-variant VCF |
| SV calling | Sniffles2 | Sorted and indexed SV VCF |
| CNV calling | mosdepth + CNVkit | Large autosomal CNV calls and 5-kb coverage track |
| Joint phasing | LongPhase | Phased SNV and SV VCFs |
| Haplotagging | LongPhase | HP-tagged BAM |
| SNV annotation | VEP + bcftools | ClinVar, gnomAD, MANE, OMIM phenotype, consequence, and homopolymer annotations |
| SV annotation | SVAFotate + VEP + MANE CDS | Population frequency, gene, phenotype, and coding-region annotations |
| Prioritization | Bundled Python scripts | Candidate TSV files |
| Visualization | igv-reports | Interactive HTML reports |
| Final report | Bundled Python script | Combined SNV/indel, SV, and CNV report |

## Candidate prioritization

The bundled scripts prioritize variants into compact candidate tables intended for rapid rare-disease review.

### SNVs and indels

Prioritization incorporates:

- ClinVar pathogenic or likely pathogenic classifications
- gnomAD maximum population allele frequency
- VEP impact and consequence
- Disease-gene membership
- MANE transcripts
- MIM morbid phenotypes
- ONT homopolymer-associated indel filtering
- Genotype, depth, VAF, quality, and phasing information

### Structural variants

Prioritization incorporates:

- Type-compatible overlap with pathogenic ClinVar SVs
- Long-read and short-read population allele frequencies
- MANE CDS overlap
- Disease-gene membership
- VEP consequence and phenotype annotation
- Resolved DEL, DUP, INS, and INV calls

Unresolved breakends are not prioritized.

### Copy-number variants

The CNV workflow targets conspicuous autosomal events of at least 50 kb. Calls must have at least 10 supporting bins and satisfy copy-number and log2-ratio thresholds.

Prioritization incorporates:

- Type-compatible overlap with pathogenic ClinVar CNVs
- DGV Gold Standard population CNVs
- Collins et al. haploinsufficiency and triplosensitivity scores
- MANE Select CDS overlap
- Patient/reference overlap fractions
- Read-depth evidence from 5-kb coverage bins

## Requirements

- Linux
- Snakemake
- Conda, Mamba, or Micromamba
- NVIDIA GPU and compatible CUDA driver for GPU-enabled Clair3 calling
- Indexed GRCh38-aligned BAM input
- External annotation bundle described below

Three reproducible environments are supplied:

- `envs/ultrarapid.yaml`
- `envs/vep.yaml`
- `envs/igvreport.yaml`

Linux package lock files are also included for stricter environment reproduction.

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tjense25/ultrarapid_pipeline.git
cd ultrarapid_pipeline
```

Copy the example configuration:

```bash
cp example.config.yml config.yml
```

Edit `config.yml` for the sample and local reference paths.

## Configuration

Example:

```yaml
sample: "example"

# Specify either bam or bam_dir.
bam: "/path/to/example.merged.bam"
# bam_dir: "/path/to/hourly_bam_directory"

fasta: "/path/to/GRCh38_no_alt_plus_hs38d1.fa"
annotation_dir: "/path/to/ultrarapid_report_annotations"

pore_version: "r10"
basecall_version: "sup"
gpus: 4
```

### Input selection

Use `bam` when the sample already has one coordinate-sorted BAM.

Use `bam_dir` to recursively discover and merge multiple BAM files before analysis. Do not retain both options in the final configuration.

### Clair3 model selection

The workflow automatically selects a Clair3 model from the pore and basecalling configuration:

| Pore | Basecalling | Clair3 model |
|---|---|---|
| R9 | HAC | `r941_prom_hac_g360+g422` |
| R9 | SUP | `r941_prom_sup_g5014` |
| R10 | HAC | `r1041_e82_400bps_hac_v500` |
| R10 | SUP | `r1041_e82_400bps_sup_v500` |

Set `gpus: 0` for CPU-only Clair3 execution.

## Annotation bundle

Large reference and annotation files are not stored in this repository. The configured `annotation_dir` must contain the expected resources, including:

- GRCh38 reference and indexes
- Clair3 model directories
- VEP 116 cache and plugins
- VEP Phenotypes plugin data
- GIAB-derived homopolymer annotations
- MANE Select CDS BED and MANE GTF
- ClinVar pathogenic SV/CNV BED files
- UWONT500 and core SVAFotate reference files
- DGV Gold Standard CNVs
- Collins et al. dosage-sensitivity scores
- Prepared IGV annotation tracks
- Default GenCC disease-gene list

A custom disease-gene file can be supplied with:

```yaml
gene_list: "/path/to/one_gene_symbol_per_line.txt"
```

If omitted, the workflow uses:

```text
ANNOTATION_DIR/GenCC_DefinitiveStrong_genelist.txt
```

## Running the pipeline

Run on a single high-performance node:

```bash
snakemake --snakefile Snakefile --configfile config.yml --use-conda --cores 224 --jobs 8 --rerun-incomplete --printshellcmds
```

Perform a dry run first:

```bash
snakemake --snakefile Snakefile --configfile config.yml --use-conda --cores 224 --jobs 8 --dry-run
```

`Snakefile_chunked` provides an alternative workflow for distributing chromosome-partitioned processing.

## Primary outputs

Outputs are written beneath the configured sample name:

```text
SAMPLE/
├── merged_bam/
├── clair3_out/
├── sniffles/
├── cnvkit/
├── longphase/
├── vep/
├── sv_anno/
├── benchmarks/
└── candidates/
```

Important final files include:

```text
SAMPLE/candidates/SAMPLE.snv_indel.candidate_variants.tsv
SAMPLE/candidates/SAMPLE.sv.candidate_variants.tsv
SAMPLE/candidates/SAMPLE.cnv.candidate_variants.tsv
SAMPLE/candidates/SAMPLE.all_candidate_variants.igv_report.html
```

The combined HTML report contains separate tabs for:

1. SNVs and indels
2. Structural variants
3. Copy-number variants
4. Filtering and tier definitions

## Benchmarking

Each major rule records runtime and resource-use information under:

```text
SAMPLE/benchmarks/
```

These files can be used to evaluate pipeline wall time and identify bottlenecks on different compute configurations.

## Important notice

This workflow is under active development and is intended for research and pipeline-evaluation use. Candidate prioritization does not constitute clinical variant classification. All reported candidates require expert review, read-level inspection, phenotype assessment, and appropriate orthogonal confirmation before clinical interpretation.
